  "notes": "Greatly extended music_catalog.json (14 -> 32 courses). Real gap fixed: MUSIC 240 (Introduction to Music Education) is the real prereq underlying MUSIC 295A/341/345/395A, but the bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan never names it directly -- it's the actual course behind that plan's generic 'Education elective' item in Year 1 Spring, added as an explicit item there. Real engine-mechanics gap (same pattern as MUSIC 122/132 in the Music B.A. build): MUSIC 345 and MUSIC 395B are mutual corequisites of each other -- broken into one-directional edges. Real gap fixed: SPLED 400 (explicitly in the bulletin's own plan) requires EDPSY 14/10/11 or HDFS 229/239, none of which the Music Education plan otherwise schedules -- added EDPSY 14 as an explicit Semester 4 item, same pattern as other majors needing SPLED 400's prereq chain filled in. The six 'MUSIC 441W-446W' emphasis courses are freely selectable per the bulletin ('select one 3-credit emphasis course'); MUSIC 443W's prereq chain runs through choral ensemble courses not modeled in this build (Ensemble is a generic slot), so the engine simply prefers one of the other five eligible emphasis options -- not a warning, just an unused alternative, same pattern as PHOTO 300/CI 312 elsewhere. Student teaching (Semester 8) is MUSIC 495A (always required, 7cr) paired with either MUSIC 495B or 495C (5cr) to total the bulletin's required 12cr -- not a mutual-corequisite pair like some other PSU student-teaching sequences, just a 'required + choose one of two' structure per the bulletin's own footnote. 'Applied Music' and 'Ensemble' (individual lessons/ensemble placement, varying by instrument) are modeled as generic slots every semester, same convention as the Music B.A. build. This plan's computed per-semester credit totals run somewhat below the bulletin's own printed ranges (roughly 116 vs. the stated 129.5 total) since 'Supporting course' and additional Gen Ed pools were sized conservatively rather than padded to force an exact match -- every named literal course and its real prereq chain is modeled correctly, which is what build_full_plan() actually verifies (0 warnings, goal met), even though the aggregate credit count is an underestimate of the real program's full load.",
